%n lūrub | ina [halbi(m)-ma | ...]
#note: See the discussion of the lines in @bib{RN271@251}. @akk{u₂-ra-ma} represents a further example of the use of D-stem instead of an expected G, typical of Akkadian texts in Ugarit (see above). The interpretation of @akk{lu?!-ru-ub} as a corrupt form of @i{lā irrub} is tentative, although it seems likely that it is a form of @i{erēbu}, as in b+25 @i{irrub}. Arnaud’s reading @akk{qu₂-ru-ub}, for @akk{qurub}, translated as “étant présent” (@bib{RN88@137}) seems less probable. The restoration @i{ina} [@i{ḫalbi}(@i{m})@i{-ma}] is made on the basis of line b+25 within the present fragment.
// cf. L I.4 SB "V" 98
// cf. L I.4 SB "V" 183
// cf. L I.4 MB "Ug₂" b+35

